orker and payments-api recover, and find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0152F26238KrgCZXvqgzdoLU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CZNQxFYwWE4YQjekxbDbhr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled back payments-worker and opened the SEV2. payments-worker has recovered, but payments-api is still showing errors.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Found the right service:** there's no service called \"payments\", but two payments services were failing in all regions at an 18% error rate: payments-worker (v3.4.0) and payments-api (v5.1.0). You confirmed the worker was the cause.\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's now healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 on payments-worker, and on-call has been paged.\n\n**Still open:** right after the rollback, payments-api was still unhealthy at 18% errors on v5.1.0. It may just need time to recover. But payments-api v5.1.0 was also a new release, and its last healthy version is v5.0.0, so the problem may be in that release too. I haven't touched payments-api. If it doesn't recover soon, I can roll it back to v5.0.0 if you want.", "type": "text"}]}]}